# .buildignore: patterns excluded from release tarballs by scripts/build-release.sh.
#
# Passed to `rsync --exclude-from` when staging server/ and scripts/ into the
# tarball. Patterns are relative to each rsync source root, not the repo root,
# so `data/` matches server/data/ (any `data/` directory at any depth).
# See rsync(1) FILTER RULES for syntax.

# Dev database and local state: would leak dev credentials and audit log
# contents into every shipped tarball. All of server/data/ is never-ship.
# (ipam.db is already caught by *.db, listing it explicitly creates a
# maintenance hazard where a future cleanup might assume it's still excluded
# via the legacy-named explicit entry.)
#
# Anchored with a leading slash to the rsync root (server/ or scripts/) so it
# matches ONLY server/data/, NOT server/src/data/, which holds shipped source
# data (doh-providers.js, device-fingerprints.js). An unanchored `data/` dropped
# server/src/data/ from the tarball → preflight ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND.
/data/
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
analytics.duckdb*

# Credentials and TLS material: belt-and-suspenders. These should be kept
# out of server/ at all times, but the exclusion catches stray dev artifacts
# if someone ever drops a key into the source tree.
#
# `*.crt` is deliberately NOT excluded because in theory someone could want
# to ship a cert in the tarball, but in practice TLS certs live only in
# /var/lib/cidrella/certs/ which isn't staged at all.
#
# `*.pub` is deliberately NOT excluded because `scripts/cidrella.pub` (the
# minisign public key) must ship in every release so update.sh can verify
# the next release's signature.
*.env
.env
.env.local
.env.production
*.key
*.pem
*.p12
*.pfx
id_rsa
id_ed25519
credentials
secrets

# Test scaffolding: not needed at runtime
tests/
vitest.config.js

# Editor/LSP indexing config: dev-only
jsconfig.json

# NOTE: scripts/ is NO LONGER filtered by this file. As of v0.4.16 its staging
# is allowlist-driven by scripts/release-files.txt, so build/dev tooling
# (build-release.sh, the check-*.js guards, deploy-lxc.sh, test-dns-blocking.sh,
# test-harness/, lint-release-notes.sh, refresh-ntp-defaults.js,
# build-releases-manifest.js, check-db-ownership.js) simply isn't listed and
# therefore never ships. The old deny-list here failed OPEN: a new dev script
# shipped unless someone remembered to add it, and four were doing exactly that.
# To change what ships from scripts/, edit scripts/release-files.txt.
#
# Everything below still applies to the server/ tree staging.

# Dev-only source files that don't belong in production. The api-browser
# route is also gated at mount time by NODE_ENV !== 'production' in
# server/src/index.js, but excluding the file here means an admin can't
# enable it in a shipped install even by monkey-patching index.js.
routes/api-browser.js

# Python bytecode cache from server/anomaly/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo

# Logs, backups, editor and OS debris
*.log
*.bak
*.tmp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/

# Dependencies: already handled by the build pipeline (server/node_modules
# is cleaned and re-installed via `npm ci --omit=dev` later), but excluded
# here as belt-and-suspenders so the dev tree's node_modules never
# accidentally makes it into staging.
node_modules/
